# Veltra Media SEO guardrails

## Project facts
- Static site generated by Node, no framework. Routes are registered in `src/pages.js`. Each page is `src/pages/*.js` exporting { path, title, description, body, jsonLd, ... }. Service pages use `serviceSalesPage()` in `src/service-sales-page.js`. Shared chrome and JSON-LD helpers are in `src/site.js`. The HTML shell is `src/layout.js`. `scripts/build.mjs` writes `dist/`, `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml` from the pages list.
- Hosting: Vercel with cleanUrls and `www` as canonical. Redirects live in BOTH `vercel.json` and `src/pages.js` (`redirects`). Keep them in sync.
- Business: Veltra Media. Services: web design, local SEO + Google Business Profile, landing pages/CRO, AI receptionist + website chat, CRM/booking automation, website care. Based in Middlesbrough, works remotely. Serves Middlesbrough, Stockton-on-Tees, Redcar, Billingham, Hartlepool and the wider Tees Valley. Language: en-GB.
- Brand collision: "Veltra" alone returns Veltra Corp (Tokyo). Always write "Veltra Media" in titles, schema and brand copy.

## Hard rules
1. NEVER invent facts: no street address, reviews, ratings, review counts, client names, case-study figures, awards, staff numbers, years trading, testimonials or "as seen in". The site publishes no address by design and tests fail if JSON-LD claims one. If a real fact is needed, put a code comment `TODO(owner): ...` and add a line to `docs/seo/owner-todo.md`. Never render TODO text into HTML.
2. NO doorway pages. Every location or service page must contain substantially unique, useful content for that place or audience. Swapping a town name into a template is not acceptable.
3. Content security policy is `script-src 'self'`. Do not add third-party or inline scripts. JSON-LD blocks are fine.
4. Every indexable page needs: a unique `<title>` (aim for 50-60 characters, never over 65), a unique meta description (120-158 characters), exactly one H1 containing the primary keyword naturally, a self-referencing canonical, an entry in the sitemap, breadcrumb markup, at least 3 contextual internal links out and at least 3 internal links in.
5. Plain UK English. No keyword stuffing, no hype ("guaranteed #1", "rank first"). Never promise rankings.
6. After every task: run `npm install` (first time only), then `npm test`, then `npm run build`. Fix anything you broke. Report pre-existing failures separately; do not hide them.
7. Do not touch `api/`, `lib/`, payments, booking, chat, voice, Stripe, Supabase or env files for SEO work.
8. Work on the current branch in small commits with clear messages. Never push, never deploy.
9. Finish every task with a report: files changed, the SEO reason for each change, how you verified it, and open owner TODOs.
